# Branch policy (hard)

Three kinds of branches: `main` (production), `dev` (staging), and short-lived
typed work branches — `feature/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `hotfix/`, `docs/`,
`sync/`. Never create a branch outside the typed set — not a scratch branch,
a worktree, or a cloud-agent branch.

## Work happens on a typed branch off `dev`

1. `git checkout dev && git pull --ff-only origin dev`.
2. `git checkout -b feature/<slug>` (or `fix/`, `chore/`, `docs/`).
3. Commit and push the work branch — `Quality` runs the full suite on it.
4. Open a PR to `dev`. Branch-policy requires the `type/slug` name.
5. **Squash merge** — one commit per feature on `dev`; head auto-deletes.
6. The merge push deploys https://dev.rive.work — the pre-production gate.

Do not commit directly to `dev`. Do not open a feature PR to `main`.

## `main` is production, merge-only

- Never commit, push, force-push, amend, or cherry-pick onto `main`.
- The only update path is a **merge commit** PR: `dev` → `main`, after
  dev.rive.work is verified.
- `git push origin main` is forbidden even when the tree looks correct.

## Hotfixes

`hotfix/<slug>` branches off `main` → PR to `main` → merge commit. Then
back-merge: `sync/main-back` off `main` → PR to `dev` → squash merge, so
staging never drifts behind production.

## Enforcement gap

The repo is private on a plan without branch protection — `main` and `dev`
cannot be locked to PR-only. The `branch-policy.yml` checks plus this rule
are the enforcement. Follow it anyway.
